THE ONE RULE
TradeBook is a two-sided marketplace, not a consumer app.
One city with 8 homes posting and 6 vendors bidding beats 80 accounts
sprayed across three states with zero awards.
Density first. Ads second. App Store last.


1. WHAT WE ARE ACTUALLY LAUNCHING
TradeBook is not a finance app, not a family funeral-home finder, and
not a Red Book clone. Funeral homes and cemeteries post work. Vendors
bid price + ETA + method (on-site or mail-in) as one offer. The home
awards. Cheapest is a sort, never an automatic award.

Job types (do not add more at launch): equipment repair / PM, removal /
transfer, trade embalming, vault / outer burial container, crematory
(retort), cooler / refrigeration.
Do not list grounds / landscaping until a cemetery actually posts it.

Live today: tradebook.co (waitlist — kill it when sit-downs start) and
app.tradebook.co (Apple + email sign-in, jobs, bids, award, Stripe seats
in TEST mode, Pay-on-TradeBook in TEST mode). Native is Expo already.
Do not start a Capacitor wrap. Repo: blackthorn1010/tradebook.
Branch: grok/tradebook-platform. Brand rules: docs/TRADEBOOK.md.

Success is NOT: App Store ranking, a national list, a TikTok audience,
or mixing TradeBook with Death Care Repair so vendors think this is
Standridge’s lead desk.

Success IS:
- Week 4: 12 homes + 12 vendors in overlapping corridor cities + 3 real awards
- Week 8: still running only if ≥ 8 real awards total
- 100 users: a living book in the Birmingham–Huntsville–Montgomery
  corridor, weekly awards. Slip the week if awards are yellow.
